# ASGI triplet — backend request path (bead enhancedchannelmanager-j9xrz + -6rrl5.1 + -6rrl5.2
# + enhancedchannelmanager-3hgrf).
#
# starlette floored at 1.6.0. The 1.3.1 floor cleared CVE-2026-48818/48817/54283/54282 (4 CVEs,
# v0.18.0 release-scan blocker) and remains the security minimum; 1.6.0 is current, and is what
# mcp-server already pins, so this converges the two services rather than diverging them.
#
# WHAT THE PIN CHAIN ACTUALLY REQUIRES. fastapi's own dependency declaration is the only hard
# link, and it is one-directional: fastapi 0.136.1 declares `starlette>=0.46.0` with no upper
# bound, so it constrains starlette's MINIMUM and nothing else. starlette may therefore move ahead
# of the version fastapi was released against, and does so here. What must never happen is
# starlette falling below fastapi's declared floor. uvicorn is not in that chain at all — nothing
# in this set depends on it; it is the server, pinned exactly for reproducibility.
#
# WHY FASTAPI IS HELD AT 0.136.1, and it is not a starlette problem. fastapi 0.137.0 stopped
# flattening included routers into `app.routes`. backend/main.py resolves a request path to its
# route template by scanning `app.routes`, and auth/mcp_capabilities.py treats an unresolved
# template as DENY — so under 0.137+ the MCP service-principal path fails closed on every route
# (proven behaviourally: 56 failures across 11 modules). The migration to `iter_route_contexts()`
# is bead enhancedchannelmanager-g4pnh, deliberately its own PR per ADR-001's one-major-bump rule.
#
# An earlier revision of this comment read "Keep this pin set aligned; a fastapi/starlette break
# must bump both at once." The project no longer follows that rule: on 2026-08-24 the PO ruled
# that starlette and uvicorn may upgrade independently of fastapi. Evidence for this pairing —
# an isolation probe (fastapi 0.136.1 + starlette 1.6.0 + uvicorn 0.52.4) ran all 11 modules that
# introspect `app.routes` green, and the full backend suite passes on the compiled lock below.
# There is precedent in this repo: bd-3hgrf moved starlette 1.0.1 -> 1.3.1 against a held fastapi
# 0.136.1 for the same reason, so the "bump both at once" wording never described actual practice.
fastapi==0.141.1
starlette>=1.6.0
uvicorn[standard]==0.52.4
