# Capped below 1.19. Alembic 1.19 added CHECK-constraint comparison to
# autogenerate, and that surfaces a real pre-existing divergence rather than a
# tool bug: migration 0012 creates ``ck_task_schedules_interval_positive``, but
# ``TaskSchedule.__table_args__`` in backend/models.py never declared it. So
# autogenerate now emits ``remove_constraint`` and
# tests/unit/test_alembic_baseline.py::test_baseline_matches_metadata_no_drift
# fails. Bisected to alembic alone: 1.18.4 passes and 1.19.1 fails with
# sqlalchemy held at 2.0.49. Lifting this cap means declaring the constraint on
# the model so metadata matches the migration DDL — a schema-correctness change
# that needs its own bead, not a currency bump.
alembic>=1.19.1,<1.20
